from common import Batch
b=Batch('NEXT',51)
def q(*args,**kw): b.add(*args,**kw)
q('S','Intercepting routes','Modal and direct navigation','How can a photo route open as a modal during in-app navigation but as a full page on a direct visit?','Combine intercepting routes with a parallel slot for the modal. Soft navigation can intercept the destination into the current layout. Direct navigation still renders the canonical full-page route.','The browser URL can identify the same resource while navigation context changes presentation. Provide dismissal and unmatched-slot behavior deliberately.','Separate canonical route from contextual presentation.','Which navigation has an existing layout to preserve?','next:app/api-reference/file-conventions/intercepting-routes')
q('M','Static generation','generateStaticParams timing','With Cache Components disabled, when is generateStaticParams used for a prerendered dynamic route?','It provides parameter combinations for build-time generation.','generateStaticParams supplies route parameters before corresponding pages are generated. It is not automatically rerun as part of ISR revalidation.','Separate enumeration from later refreshes.','Does revalidation enumerate the entire route set again?','next:app/api-reference/functions/generate-static-params',wrong=['It runs after every client click in the browser.','It replaces authorization checks for every parameter.','It automatically reruns during every ISR revalidation.'])
q('C','Errors','Segment error boundary','What are the scope and component requirements of error.js in the App Router?','It is a Client Component error boundary for the appropriate nested segment subtree. It can offer retry UI. Errors in the same segment’s layout require a boundary above that layout rather than relying on its own error.js.','Boundary placement follows nesting. A root-level global-error file has a separate role for failures outside ordinary segment boundaries.','Ask which subtree the boundary wraps.','Is the failing layout above or below it?','next:app/api-reference/file-conventions/error')
q('W','Errors','Not-found route UI','Write app/not-found.jsx with a heading and a Link back to the home page.','import Link from "next/link";\n\nexport default function NotFound() {\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Page not found</h1>\n      <Link href="/">Go home</Link>\n    </main>\n  );\n}','The file supplies missing-resource UI.~The Link gives a recovery path.~The framework controls status handling; a streamed response may already have sent headers, so do not infer its HTTP status solely from visible fallback text.','Use the not-found file convention.','Offer a useful navigation recovery.','next:app/api-reference/file-conventions/not-found','// Implement app/not-found.jsx.')
q('S','Streaming','Parallel data requests','Two independent server fetches are awaited one after the other. How do you avoid that data waterfall without hiding failures?','Start both operations before awaiting their combined results. Use Promise.all when both must succeed. Place Suspense boundaries according to which results can render independently.','Starting work concurrently reduces serial waiting. Promise.all does not cancel a sibling operation when one rejects, and dependent requests cannot simply be parallelized.','Identify true dependencies.','Can both requests start now?','next:app/getting-started/fetching-data#parallel-data-fetching')
q('B','Components','Serializable client props','Why is passing this ordinary server-created callback to a Client Component invalid?','Ordinary server closures are not serializable client props. Define the interaction in the Client Component or pass a supported Server Function for a server operation.','The server creates a closure over server execution state.~The client boundary needs supported serializable values or a recognized server reference.~A normal function is not automatically converted into a Server Action.','Crossing the boundary requires a transport representation.','Was the function declared as a Server Function?','next:app/api-reference/directives/use-client#usage','// Server Component\nexport default function Page() {\n  return <ClientButton onClick={() => console.log("clicked")} />;\n}')
q('C','Actions','Mutation transport','Why should a Server Action be treated as a server endpoint even if the source looks like a function call?','The client invocation crosses a network boundary. The server executes the function with serialized inputs. Validate input, permissions and failure behavior as with any mutation endpoint.','A function-like API does not imply a trusted in-process caller. Current Server Actions use POST for invocation, but method choice alone is not authorization.','The syntax hides transport.','Which values can the caller control?','next:app/getting-started/mutating-data')
q('S','Metadata','Streaming metadata','Can current App Router metadata always be assumed to block all visible page content?','No, dynamic metadata can be streamed for supported clients. Next.js adjusts behavior for HTML-limited bots that require metadata in the head before content. Avoid assuming one response timing model for every user agent.','Metadata streaming changes delivery timing, not the need for correct metadata. Test relevant crawlers and configuration rather than inferring behavior from a browser alone.','Rendering can stream more than body content.','Do all clients process streamed metadata equally?','next:app/api-reference/functions/generate-metadata#streaming-metadata')
q('M','Images','Current image preloading','In current Next.js 16, which next/image prop explicitly preloads a known LCP image when preload is appropriate?','preload','preload is the current explicit preload prop. The priority prop is deprecated in Next.js 16; do not preload every image or combine conflicting loading strategies indiscriminately.','Use the current prop name.','Only the critical image should need this treatment.','next:app/api-reference/components/image#preload',wrong=['priority','preloadAll','blocking'])
q('B','Dynamic imports','ssr false placement','Why is this client-only dynamic import invalid in a Server Component module?','ssr: false is supported in Client Components. Move the dynamic declaration into a module marked "use client" and render that wrapper from the server.','The option disables server rendering of that client-loaded component.~A Server Component cannot use this option directly.~The wrapper gives the browser-only dependency an explicit client boundary.','The option belongs to a client loading boundary.','Which module owns the browser-only import?','next:app/guides/lazy-loading#skipping-ssr','import dynamic from "next/dynamic";\nconst Chart = dynamic(() => import("./Chart"), { ssr: false });\n\nexport default function Page() {\n  return <Chart />;\n}')
q('A','Deployment','Static export constraints','Can a static export support request-time authenticated Server Actions without a server runtime?','No, static output cannot execute request-time server mutations by itself. Use a server deployment or a separate API with an explicit client integration. Choose hosting according to the features the app actually uses.','Build-time generated files are not an execution environment for future Server Actions. Browser code cannot safely inherit server secrets just because hosting is static.','A static host serves files.','Where would the server function execute?','next:app/guides/static-exports#unsupported-features')
q('C','Runtime','Node and Edge dependencies','Why must a package be checked before running it in the Edge runtime?','Edge exposes a more limited runtime API set than Node.js. Packages that require unsupported Node facilities can fail. Choose a compatible dependency or the Node runtime for that workload.','TypeScript compilation does not guarantee runtime API availability. A package may indirectly depend on unsupported functionality even when its public interface looks portable.','Check transitive runtime requirements.','Does the package assume Node-only APIs?','next:app/api-reference/edge')
q('U','Caching','Cache key inputs','Follow-up to NEXT-033: why must every value affecting cached output be represented in the cache identity?','Otherwise distinct requests can reuse the wrong result. Serializable arguments and relevant captured inputs participate in use cache key construction. Keep hidden mutable global dependencies out of cached calculations or explicitly invalidate them.','A cache is correct only for its declared inputs and freshness policy. Tags label entries for invalidation; they do not replace the cache key.','A tag and a key solve different problems.','Could two different inputs collide?','next:app/api-reference/directives/use-cache#cache-keys')
q('S','Security','Proxy authorization coverage','Why is a Proxy redirect insufficient as the only authorization check for protected Server Functions?','Matchers can exclude requests and route refactors can change coverage. Each protected operation should validate its caller and resource access. Proxy can provide early navigation behavior but should not own all data authorization.','Server Functions are invoked through route POST requests, not a separately guaranteed Proxy namespace. UI and routing checks can be bypassed as data protection.','Authorize where data is accessed.','Can the matcher omit a mutation route?','next:app/api-reference/file-conventions/proxy#execution-order')
q('A','Architecture','Server and client composition','Design a catalog page with server-loaded product details and a small interactive favorite button. How should the component boundary be placed?','Keep product fetching and noninteractive details on the server. Put only the favorite interaction in a Client Component with minimal supported props. Use an authorized server mutation for persistence and an explicit refresh or invalidation policy.','A client wrapper can receive server-rendered children without importing their implementation into its client graph. Boundary placement affects bundle size and secret exposure.','Find the smallest interactive island.','Which data must actually cross to the browser?','next:app/getting-started/server-and-client-components#interleaving-server-and-client-components')
